  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. For each valid iii, the star value of the element AiA_iAi​ is the number of valid indices j&lt;ij \\lt ij&lt;i such that AjA_jAj​ is divisible by AiA_iAi​.\n\nChef is a curious person, so he wants to know the maximum star value in the given sequence. Help him find it.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\le N \\le 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1061 \\le A_i \\le 10^61≤Ai​≤106 for each valid iii",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 100,000100,000100,000.",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (20 points):** sum  of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5,0005,0005,000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT which denotes the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN .\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the maximum star value.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n7\n8 1 28 4 2 6 7",
        "output": "3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nA5=2A_5 = 2A5​=2 divides 444, 282828 and 888, so its star value is 333. There is no element with a higher star value."
      }
    ]
  },
